loads** (Distributed Workloads team): passive — the\n  strategy requires no code change to it; the Kueue quota model\n  (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue) is consumed as-is by the admin view. Because the\n  validating team differs from the epic that touches it, the passive-component\n  validation is a separate Implementation epic owned by the Distributed\n  Workloads team (per the Step 2 exception).\n- Both components exist in `.context/architecture-context/` and are Konflux\n  onboarded — no onboarding chain (repo/license/konflux) is generated.\n- The metering data source itself is owned by the in-flight RHAISTRAT-9990\n  strategy and has no canonical RHAI component in `.context/rhai-components.txt`\n  (the closest consumer-side canonical name, `Dashboard`, is used for the\n  investigation that validates the contract). This mapping is noted here as\n  non-obvious.\n\n## Step 3 — unknowns scan\n\nThe strategy's single flagged open question: the metering data schema\nfinalizes only when RHAISTRAT-9990 lands. Decision rule: the answer changes\nwhat the reporting backend does (its data-access and computation design), so it\nis a genuine unknown → **Investigation epic E001** validating the metering data\ncontract. Its outcome is a true gate on the reporting backend\n(`gate_failure_impact: rewrite` — an aggregation/adaptation layer is added if\nthe contract lacks native per-project attribution or time-range granularity).\n\nNo conditional branch files were written: the bounded outcomes\n(contract-consumable-as-is vs. contract-needs-adaptation) change the *scope* of\nthe same downstream epic (rewrite), not which epics exist — the main plan\ncovers the primary path and the deviation is recorded as the gate's fallback.\n\nNo other unknowns: HLR-2's \"stable API\" placement is API-surface discovery, an\nimplementation detail (AC + health warning below), not a structural unknown.\nKueue quota semantics are corroborated by architecture context, not open.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n| RHAISTRAT-9018-E001 | Validate the GPU usage metering data contract for chargeback reporting | Investigation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9018-E002 | GPU chargeback reporting backend: per-project GPU-hour reports, CSV export, and stable API | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 | Dashboard admin view for GPU chargeback reports and Kueue quota comparison | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9018-E004 | Validate Kueue quota attribution in the GPU chargeback admin view | Implementation | Distributed Workloads | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-9018-E005 | Document GPU chargeback report semantics and export integration | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[RHAISTRAT-9018-E001 Investigation: metering data contract] --> E002[RHAISTRAT-9018-E002 Reporting backend + export/API]\n    E002 --> E003[RHAISTRAT-9018-E003 Admin view: reports vs Kueue quota]\n    E003 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9018-E004 DW validation of quota attribution]\n    E002 --> E005[RHAISTRAT-9018-E005 Docs]\n    E003 --> E005\n    E004 --> E005\n```\n\nCritical path: E001 → E002 → E003 → E004 → E005 (length 5).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation gate) | The metering data contract determines the reporting backend's data-access and computation design; outcome rewrites E002 scope if attribution/granularity is not natively supported. True gate recorded as `gated_by` + `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite` on E002. |\n| E002 → E003 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The admin UI builds against the reporting backend's report-data API; the backend produces the artifact the frontend consumes. |\n| E003 → E004 | Step 2 passive-component exception | Distributed Workloads is passive (no code changes); the owning team's validation epic verifies the quota attribution implemented in the admin view, so it runs after the view exists. |\n| E002 → E005, E003 → E005, E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes what was built; blocked by every Implementation epic. |\n\nNon-edges (parallelism rationale): none of the Rules 7/8/10 pairs apply — no\nrepo/license/konflux onboarding epics exist (both components are already\nonboarded per architecture context). E001 is not an edge into E003/E004/E005\ndirectly: its effect flows transitively through E002.\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n| HLR-1 (per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges) | P0 | E002, E003 | Backend computation + admin UI presentation of the same report surface. |\n| HLR-2 (CSV export + stable API for finance tooling) | P1 | E002 (bundled) | Bundled into the P0 reporting backend: the export and API are delivery modes of the same report data structures and endpoints HLR-1 builds — the same per-project GPU-hour aggregation over time ranges serves the UI, the CSV, and the API. Splitting would build the same computation and API surface twice and add an artificial serialization edge between two epics owning one surface. Not independently deferrable. |\n| HLR-3 (admin view: current-month consumption vs Kueue quota) | P1 | E003 (bundled), E004 | Bundled into the P0 admin view epic: the quota comparison renders in the same admin view/UI surface as the HLR-1 report tables (same screen, same per-project rows, same data-fetch path); a separate epic would rebuild the same view. E004 is the Distributed Workloads team's validation of the quota attribution (passive-component exception), not a second implementation. |\n| HLR-4 (documentation of report semantics and export integration) | P2 | E005 | docs-authoring epic; priority derived from strategy `priority: Major` → P1 (docs-authoring priority exception — it does not push P0 upstream). |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): Impacted Teams table,\n   Dependencies table, formal Acceptance Criteria, and NFRs are absent; teams\n   were inferred from architecture context and ACs derived from HLR text.\n2. **Scope trap / architecture tension on HLR-2**: the Dashboard architecture\n   context (`architecture/rhoai-3.0/dashboard.md`) states the Dashboard exposes\n   \"Kubernetes API only; no private component APIs\" and \"owns no data plane\",\n   while HLR-2 requires a stable API for finance tooling. Where that API is\n   served is unresolved by the strategy; per the unclear-passage rule this is\n   API-surface discovery (implementation detail) captured as an AC on E002\n   (documented, versioned API contract), but reviewers should confirm the\n   placement decision does not spawn a new component epic later.\n3. **External timing risk** (not an AC — externally controlled): the entire P0\n   chain is gated on the RHAISTRAT-9990 metering schema finalizing. E001\n   front-loads the risk by validating the contract early; the timing itself\n   belongs to the other strategy and is recorded in E001/E002 Risks.\n4. **Priority check**: no inversions found. E003 is P0 because it carries\n   HLR-1's P0 UI surface (HLR-3's P1 is bundled, see matrix). E004 is P1 — it\n   enables only HLR-3. E005 is P1 via the docs-authoring priority exception\n   (Major → P1), exempt from inheritance.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nEvaluated per Step 5.5 for the external dependency (RHAISTRAT-9990, in flight,\nuncertain timing): the strategy cannot deliver independent user-facing partial\nvalue without the metering data — every HLR-1/2/3 surface renders consumption\nfigures computed from it, and the quota validation (E004) verifies the\nimplemented view. Therefore no Tier 1/Tier 2 split: linear dependencies with\nthe external dependency blocking downstream, mitigated by the E001\nrisk-reduction investigation at the front of the chain.\n\n## Epic-size check\n\nAll epics are within the ~2-week guideline; no overage handling needed.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39467,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dee8d39a363c00d","agent_id":"ae32d1b8c5297bda1","session_id":"2c7f7242-e955-423b-a303-ec17bb0be124","uuid":"620b1054-4817-4dab-8710-f49de15a7ccb","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:29:39.382Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 into epics"}
