{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-2b9723af-b8dd-4c00-8772-6694a26ded3e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b647f98c1c551560","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-uzjl6zgc/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E001.md","content":"# Validate the GPU usage metering data contract for chargeback reporting\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the strategy's flagged open question: the GPU\nusage metering data schema is owned by the in-flight GPU usage metering\nstrategy (RHAISTRAT-9990) and is not final until that strategy lands. Before\nthe chargeback reporting backend is built, this investigation validates the\nmetering data contract — schema, access path, update cadence — and determines\nwhether it natively supports the reporting needs: per-project GPU-hour\nattribution, arbitrary selectable time ranges, and current-month aggregation.\n\nThe outcome gates the reporting backend implementation: if the contract is\nconsumable as-is, the backend proceeds as planned; if it lacks per-project\nattribution or the required time granularity, the backend's scope is rewritten\nto add an aggregation/adaptation layer over the raw metering data.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Document the metering data contract as delivered or planned by the GPU usage\n  metering strategy: data schema, access path, refresh cadence, and ownership.\n- For each reporting need, determine and record one of: natively supported /\n  derivable with adaptation / missing:\n  - per-project GPU-hour attribution;\n  - consumption queries over arbitrary selectable time ranges;\n  - current-month (month-to-date) aggregation.\n- Identify how the reporting side should consume the data without\n  re-implementing collection (consumption interface, not collection).\n- Produce a go/no-go recommendation with an adaptation approach sufficient to\n  scope the reporting backend without further discovery.\n- Record the finalization timing risk and a re-check trigger tied to the\n  metering strategy's landing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The metering data contract (schema, access path, cadence) is documented,\n  including the fields relevant to per-project GPU-hour attribution and\n  time-range queries.\n- Every reporting need listed in Scope carries an explicit determination\n  (natively supported / derivable with adaptation / missing) with evidence.\n- A written go/no-go recommendation exists that is sufficient to finalize the\n  reporting backend's scope, including the adaptation approach if any\n  determination is not natively supported.\n- The consumption approach is documented and demonstrably does not re-implement\n  metering collection.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): this investigation de-risks the data foundation for per-project\n  GPU-hour consumption reports; its outcome determines the data-access design\n  of the reporting backend that implements HLR-1.\n\n## Risks\n\n- The metering schema is externally owned and finalizes only when the metering\n  strategy lands; finalization timing is outside this strategy's control and\n  may extend the gate. The investigation records a re-check trigger rather\n  than assuming a fixed date.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42028,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dee8d39a363c00d","agent_id":"ae32d1b8c5297bda1","session_id":"2c7f7242-e955-423b-a303-ec17bb0be124","uuid":"647f8a00-bfb6-42bb-9ef6-b8cd4b82dc1f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:29:49.914Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 into epics"}
