{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-aaac3631-32d3-4faf-a8b4-7ee5060152fb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a11a2734562816e4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-uzjl6zgc/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E002.md","content":"# GPU chargeback reporting backend: per-project GPU-hour reports, CSV export, and stable API\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the reporting backend for GPU chargeback: computation of\nper-project GPU-hour consumption over selectable time ranges from the metering\ndata delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990), plus the\ndelivery surfaces for that report data — retrieval by the Dashboard admin view,\nCSV export, and a stable API for finance tooling. Reports are denominated in\nGPU-hours; no currency/cost-rate modelling. Collection is not re-implemented:\nconsumption is isolated behind the metering data contract validated by the\nupstream investigation.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Per-project GPU-hour report computation over arbitrary selectable time\n  ranges, computed from the metering data (consumption only — no collection).\n- Current-month (month-to-date) aggregation per project, consumed by the admin\n  view.\n- Report data access for the Dashboard admin view.\n- CSV export of reports.\n- Stable, documented API for retrieving reports, suitable for finance tooling\n  integration.\n- A documented, versioned contract for the report data and the retrieval API,\n  so the admin view and finance tooling build against a stable interface.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given metering data covering a time range, the backend returns per-project\n  GPU-hour totals for that range (and month-to-date totals for the current\n  month), matching the metering source within a documented tolerance.\n- Reports are exportable as CSV and the export round-trips the same figures\n  shown in the admin view.\n- Reports are retrievable via the documented, versioned API, and the API\n  contract is published so finance tooling can integrate against it without\n  change tracking guesswork.\n- Metering consumption is isolated behind the validated metering data\n  contract; no metering collection logic is implemented in this codebase.\n- Report figures are in GPU-hours with no currency conversion.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time\n  ranges — the backend computation and report-data surface.\n- HLR-2 (P1, bundled): CSV export and stable API for finance tooling — bundled\n  with HLR-1 because the export and API are delivery modes of the same\n  per-project GPU-hour aggregation and report endpoints the P0 work builds;\n  splitting would build the same surface twice.\n\n## Risks\n\n- The metering data schema finalizes only when RHAISTRAT-9990 lands; this epic\n  is gated on the validated contract and carries that external timing risk.\n- Where the stable API is served is an open implementation decision (the\n  Dashboard's architecture context notes it exposes Kubernetes API only); the\n  placement must be resolved when designing the versioned contract, and is\n  flagged in the decomposition summary's health warnings.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42809,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dee8d39a363c00d","agent_id":"ae32d1b8c5297bda1","session_id":"2c7f7242-e955-423b-a303-ec17bb0be124","uuid":"415c0fba-d5e1-488f-86f7-1e0c636cfebd","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:29:59.746Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 into epics"}
