{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-2c223669-fb69-4476-b3a7-a872475d6bae","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-be6ee02e077cb9ba","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-uzjl6zgc/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E003.md","content":"# Dashboard admin view for GPU chargeback reports and Kueue quota comparison\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the administrator-facing Dashboard view for GPU chargeback\nreporting: per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time\nranges, and the current-month consumption of each project shown against its\nKueue quota. It builds against the report data and API contract delivered by\nthe reporting backend. The view is restricted to platform administrators.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Admin view listing per-project GPU-hour consumption with admin-selectable\n  time ranges, rendered from the reporting backend's report data.\n- Current-month (month-to-date) consumption displayed against each project's\n  Kueue quota (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model), with the quota\n  attribution rules the view applies documented for validation by the\n  Distributed Workloads team.\n- Administrator-only visibility of the chargeback view, consistent with the\n  Dashboard's OpenShift OAuth / RBAC model.\n- Report export entry point (CSV) surfaced in the admin view, using the\n  backend's export capability.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- An administrator can select a time range and see per-project GPU-hour\n  consumption for that range, matching the reporting backend's figures for the\n  same range.\n- The view shows each project's current-month consumption alongside its Kueue\n  quota, and the quota attribution rules used (which queue-level quota is\n  attributed to which project) are documented.\n- The chargeback view is not visible to non-administrator users.\n- CSV export of the displayed report is available from the admin view and\n  round-trips the same figures.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0): the administrator-facing presentation of per-project GPU-hour\n  consumption reports over selectable time ranges.\n- HLR-3 (P1, bundled): current-month consumption against each project's Kueue\n  quota — bundled with HLR-1 because it renders in the same admin view, same\n  per-project rows, and same report-data fetch path; a separate epic would\n  rebuild the same UI surface.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Distributed Workloads requires no code change for this view; its quota model\n  is consumed read-only. The quota attribution implemented here is validated\n  by the Distributed Workloads team as a follow-on validation epic, which this\n  view supports by documenting its attribution rules.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":43599,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dee8d39a363c00d","agent_id":"ae32d1b8c5297bda1","session_id":"2c7f7242-e955-423b-a303-ec17bb0be124","uuid":"330d45bf-4028-4ba1-8c58-d9469524adb5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:30:08.161Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 into epics"}
