ttribution and the Kueue quota\n  semantics is documented with severity and a recommended correction.\n- The report states whether Distributed Workloads needs any code change for\n  the chargeback view, with supporting evidence.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1): the admin view shows current-month consumption against each\n  project's Kueue quota — this epic is the Distributed Workloads team's\n  validation of that quota attribution (passive-component validation owned by\n  the component's team).\n\n## Notes\n\n- The admin view's quota attribution rules are documented by the Dashboard\n  implementation as an input to this validation.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44276,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dee8d39a363c00d","agent_id":"ae32d1b8c5297bda1","session_id":"2c7f7242-e955-423b-a303-ec17bb0be124","uuid":"fda056a6-b4fb-47ad-97ab-c113ac5bbf9e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:30:16.958Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018 into epics"}
