{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a11faba53741db9e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate the GPU usage metering data contract for chargeback reporting\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Validate the GPU usage metering data contract for chargeback reporting\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's flagged open question: the GPU\n30\tusage metering data schema is owned by the in-flight GPU usage metering\n31\tstrategy (RHAISTRAT-9990) and is not final until that strategy lands. Before\n32\tthe chargeback reporting backend is built, this investigation validates the\n33\tmetering data contract — schema, access path, update cadence — and determines\n34\twhether it natively supports the reporting needs: per-project GPU-hour\n35\tattribution, arbitrary selectable time ranges, and current-month aggregation.\n36\t\n37\tThe outcome gates the reporting backend implementation: if the contract is\n38\tconsumable as-is, the backend proceeds as planned; if it lacks per-project\n39\tattribution or the required time granularity, the backend's scope is rewritten\n40\tto add an aggregation/adaptation layer over the raw metering data.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Document the metering data contract as delivered or planned by the GPU usage\n45\t  metering strategy: data schema, access path, refresh cadence, and ownership.\n46\t- For each reporting need, determine and record one of: natively supported /\n47\t  derivable with adaptation / missing:\n48\t  - per-project GPU-hour attribution;\n49\t  - consumption queries over arbitrary selectable time ranges;\n50\t  - current-month (month-to-date) aggregation.\n51\t- Identify how the reporting side should consume the data without\n52\t  re-implementing collection (consumption interface, not collection).\n53\t- Produce a go/no-go recommendation with an adaptation approach sufficient to\n54\t  scope the reporting backend without further discovery.\n55\t- Record the finalization timing risk and a re-check trigger tied to the\n56\t  metering strategy's landing.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- The metering data contract (schema, access path, cadence) is documented,\n61\t  including the fields relevant to per-project GPU-hour attribution and\n62\t  time-range queries.\n63\t- Every reporting need listed in Scope carries an explicit determination\n64\t  (natively supported / derivable with adaptation / missing) with evidence.\n65\t- A written go/no-go recommendation exists that is sufficient to finalize the\n66\t  reporting backend's scope, including the adaptation approach if any\n67\t  determination is not natively supported.\n68\t- The consumption approach is documented and demonstrably does not re-implement\n69\t  metering collection.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-1 (P0): this investigation de-risks the data foundation for per-project\n74\t  GPU-hour consumption reports; its outcome determines the data-access design\n75\t  of the reporting backend that implements HLR-1.\n76\t\n77\t## Risks\n78\t\n79\t- The metering schema is externally owned and finalizes only when the metering\n80\t  strategy lands; finalization timing is outside this strategy's control and\n81\t  may extend the gate. The investigation records a re-check trigger rather\n82\t  than assuming a fixed date.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a85c2b9d083d1e57","agent_id":"a03579676fb753c67","session_id":"2c7f7242-e955-423b-a303-ec17bb0be124","uuid":"ee888459-87b8-4594-9d07-5339dd30b5a1","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:31:45.423Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a11faba53741db9e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
