{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b535065b0e8a9293","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n3\ttitle: 'GPU chargeback reporting backend: per-project GPU-hour reports, CSV export,\n4\t  and stable API'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n6\tcomponent: Dashboard\n7\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9018-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the metering data contract lacks native per-project GPU-hour\n16\t    attribution or time-range granularity, rewrite the reporting backend scope to\n17\t    add an aggregation/adaptation layer over the raw metering data; if the contract\n18\t    is not yet final, the epic remains blocked on the metering strategy landing.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 0\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: -1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Low\n32\tai_implementability_score: -2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# GPU chargeback reporting backend: per-project GPU-hour reports, CSV export, and stable API\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tThis epic delivers the reporting backend for GPU chargeback: computation of\n41\tper-project GPU-hour consumption over selectable time ranges from the metering\n42\tdata delivered by the GPU usage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990), plus the\n43\tdelivery surfaces for that report data — retrieval by the Dashboard admin view,\n44\tCSV export, and a stable API for finance tooling. Reports are denominated in\n45\tGPU-hours; no currency/cost-rate modelling. Collection is not re-implemented:\n46\tconsumption is isolated behind the metering data contract validated by the\n47\tupstream investigation.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Per-project GPU-hour report computation over arbitrary selectable time\n52\t  ranges, computed from the metering data (consumption only — no collection).\n53\t- Current-month (month-to-date) aggregation per project, consumed by the admin\n54\t  view.\n55\t- Report data access for the Dashboard admin view.\n56\t- CSV export of reports.\n57\t- Stable, documented API for retrieving reports, suitable for finance tooling\n58\t  integration.\n59\t- A documented, versioned contract for the report data and the retrieval API,\n60\t  so the admin view and finance tooling build against a stable interface.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- Given metering data covering a time range, the backend returns per-project\n65\t  GPU-hour totals for that range (and month-to-date totals for the current\n66\t  month), matching the metering source within a documented tolerance.\n67\t- Reports are exportable as CSV and the export round-trips the same figures\n68\t  shown in the admin view.\n69\t- Reports are retrievable via the documented, versioned API, and the API\n70\t  contract is published so finance tooling can integrate against it without\n71\t  change tracking guesswork.\n72\t- Metering consumption is isolated behind the validated metering data\n73\t  contract; no metering collection logic is implemented in this codebase.\n74\t- Report figures are in GPU-hours with no currency conversion.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- HLR-1 (P0): per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time\n79\t  ranges — the backend computation and report-data surface.\n80\t- HLR-2 (P1, bundled): CSV export and stable API for finance tooling — bundled\n81\t  with HLR-1 because the export and API are delivery modes of the same\n82\t  per-project GPU-hour aggregation and report endpoints the P0 work builds;\n83\t  splitting would build the same surface twice.\n84\t\n85\t## Risks\n86\t\n87\t- The metering data schema finalizes only when RHAISTRAT-9990 lands; this epic\n88\t  is gated on the validated contract and carries that external timing risk.\n89\t- Where the stable API is served is an open implementation decision (the\n90\t  Dashboard's architecture context notes it exposes Kubernetes API only); the\n91\t  placement must be resolved when designing the versioned contract, and is\n92\t  flagged in the decomposition summary's health warnings.\n93\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a85c2b9d083d1e57","agent_id":"a03579676fb753c67","session_id":"2c7f7242-e955-423b-a303-ec17bb0be124","uuid":"ab62c6ee-4dde-4de5-8c91-2f8146c35600","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:31:46.209Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b535065b0e8a9293","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
