{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af591c23e24a7757","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E004\n3\ttitle: Validate Kueue quota attribution in the GPU chargeback admin view\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Distributed Workloads\n6\tteam: Distributed Workloads\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E003\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 0\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 4\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Validate Kueue quota attribution in the GPU chargeback admin view\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThe Distributed Workloads component is a passive party to this strategy: no\n35\tcode changes are made to it, and its Kueue quota model (ClusterQueue/LocalQueue)\n36\tis consumed as-is by the Dashboard's chargeback admin view. Because the\n37\tvalidating team differs from the team that builds the view, this epic delivers\n38\tthe Distributed Workloads team's validation of the quota attribution shown in\n39\tthe admin view: that each project's displayed Kueue quota and the\n40\tconsumption-versus-quota comparison correctly reflect the platform's queueing\n41\tand quota semantics.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Validate the per-project quota attribution implemented in the chargeback\n46\t  admin view against the Kueue ClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model: which\n47\t  queue-level quota is attributed to which project, and how nominal quota,\n48\t  usage, and borrowing are represented in the comparison.\n49\t- Validate the current-month consumption-versus-quota comparison semantics for\n50\t  representative project/quota configurations.\n51\t- Produce a validation report with pass/fail per scenario, discrepancies with\n52\t  severity, and recommended corrections to the view's attribution rules.\n53\t- Confirm (or record findings to the contrary) that Distributed Workloads\n54\t  requires no code changes to support the chargeback reporting view.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A validation report exists covering the admin view's per-project quota\n59\t  attribution and consumption-versus-quota comparison, with an explicit\n60\t  pass/fail result per validated scenario.\n61\t- Every discrepancy between the view's attribution and the Kueue quota\n62\t  semantics is documented with severity and a recommended correction.\n63\t- The report states whether Distributed Workloads needs any code change for\n64\t  the chargeback view, with supporting evidence.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- HLR-3 (P1): the admin view shows current-month consumption against each\n69\t  project's Kueue quota — this epic is the Distributed Workloads team's\n70\t  validation of that quota attribution (passive-component validation owned by\n71\t  the component's team).\n72\t\n73\t## Notes\n74\t\n75\t- The admin view's quota attribution rules are documented by the Dashboard\n76\t  implementation as an input to this validation.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a85c2b9d083d1e57","agent_id":"a03579676fb753c67","session_id":"2c7f7242-e955-423b-a303-ec17bb0be124","uuid":"1d2181ce-6f9b-4226-accc-95dbce729c37","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:31:47.695Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-af591c23e24a7757","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
