{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2d105211b8e95fb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9018-E005\n3\ttitle: Document GPU chargeback report semantics and export integration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9018\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E002\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E003\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9018-E004\n14\tai_signals:\n15\t  change_specificity: 1\n16\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n17\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n18\t  existing_foundation: 0\n19\t  open_questions: 0\n20\t  external_dependency: 0\n21\t  human_process_gates: -1\n22\t  repo_access: 0\n23\t  architecture_claims: 0\n24\tinvestigation_signals: null\n25\tai_implementability: Medium\n26\tai_implementability_score: 0\n27\tjira_key: null\n28\tbranch: null\n29\tgated_by: null\n30\tgate_failure_impact: null\n31\t---\n32\t# Document GPU chargeback report semantics and export integration\n33\t\n34\t## Description\n35\t\n36\tThis epic delivers the administrator and finance-tooling documentation for GPU\n37\tchargeback reporting: what the reports mean — in particular what counts as a\n38\tbillable GPU-hour and how consumption is attributed to projects — and how to\n39\tintegrate with the export surfaces (CSV and the stable report retrieval API).\n40\tIt documents what was built, and therefore runs after the reporting\n41\timplementation and validation are complete.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Documentation of report semantics:\n46\t  - definition of a GPU-hour as reported (what counts, rounding/aggregation\n47\t    behavior, tolerance versus the metering source);\n48\t  - per-project attribution rules, including the Kueue quota attribution used\n49\t    in the current-month comparison;\n50\t  - time-range semantics of the reports (selectable ranges, month-to-date).\n51\t- Documentation of export integration:\n52\t  - CSV export usage and format;\n53\t  - integration guide for finance tooling against the stable report\n54\t    retrieval API and its versioned contract.\n55\t- Coverage of administrator tasks: viewing reports, selecting time ranges,\n56\t  exporting.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Published documentation defines what counts as a GPU-hour in the reports and\n61\t  the per-project attribution rules, consistent with the implemented reporting\n62\t  backend and the validated quota attribution.\n63\t- Published documentation covers CSV export and finance-tooling integration\n64\t  against the report retrieval API, with examples a finance-tooling\n65\t  integration can follow.\n66\t- The documentation has been technically reviewed against the implemented\n67\t  reporting backend, admin view, and validation findings, and any review\n68\t  findings are addressed.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation covers report semantics (what counts as a\n73\t  GPU-hour) and export integration.\n74\t\n75\t## Notes\n76\t\n77\t- Priority derived from the strategy's `priority: Major` (docs-authoring\n78\t  priority exception): P1. Report semantics content must reflect the metering\n79\t  consumption contract and the Distributed Workloads team's validated quota\n80\t  attribution, hence the dependency on all implementation epics.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a85c2b9d083d1e57","agent_id":"a03579676fb753c67","session_id":"2c7f7242-e955-423b-a303-ec17bb0be124","uuid":"5ac0f1ca-84ea-4ca6-b6b8-fb93ba04974c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:31:48.372Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2d105211b8e95fb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
