No work-product type mixing — content authoring is\n63\tisolated in E005. All epics fit the ~2-week guideline; E002 (computation + CSV + API +\n64\tversioned contract) is one logical change over one backend surface, not a heterogeneous\n65\tmonolith.\n66\t\n67\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n68\tE001 is a genuine Investigation: its outcome (contract consumable vs. needs adaptation)\n69\trewrites E002's scope, and E002 records gated_by=E001 (present in its direct dependencies)\n70\twith a fully populated gate_failure_impact (action + fallback_approach). E002–E005 are\n71\tImplementations that each produce a concrete artifact (backend code, admin view, validation\n72\treport, published docs). No epic lists an Investigation in dependencies without gated_by;\n73\tno scheduling dependency is misfiled as a gate. E004 as an Implementation (validation\n74\tdeliverable) is correct — its report is an artifact, and its findings are follow-on\n75\tcorrections, not a structural gate.\n76\t\n77\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n78\tType-appropriate signal fields throughout: E001 carries investigation_signals (null\n79\tai_signals); E002–E005 carry ai_signals (null investigation_signals); all five ai-signals\n80\trationale files exist and match the frontmatter values. E001's source_accessibility: 0 is\n81\tcorrectly scored — the final schema does not exist yet in any readable artifact.\n82\tCalibration against .context holds up: E002's architecture_claims: -1 correctly catches\n83\tthe tension between HLR-2's stable API and dashboard.md's \"Kubernetes API only; no private\n84\tcomponent APIs / owns no data plane\" (verified in the context file); E003's and E004's\n85\tarchitecture_claims: 1 cite corroborating context (Dashboard console/OAuth RBAC; Kueue\n86\tClusterQueue/LocalQueue quota model, verified). E005's architecture_claims: 0 was checked:\n87\tits component (Documentation) has no architecture-context file, and its content mirrors\n88\twhat E002–E004 built rather 